  <revision rev="1" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>89cf698dcca6922aa20f09fc1eca2a89</srcmd5>
    <version>0.0.21</version>
    <time>1788270418</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>New package: gnss-sdr, a software-defined receiver for GNSS signals (GPS L1/L2C/L5,
GLONASS L1/L2, BeiDou B1I/B3I, Galileo E1b/c/E5a), maintained in hardware:sdr.

This is a _multibuild source package, so it is ONE Factory package with two build
flavours:

  flavour &quot;&quot;      -&gt; gnss-sdr
  flavour &quot;volk&quot;  -&gt; gnss-sdr-volk, gnss-sdr-volk-devel, libvolk_gnsssdr0_0_21

volk_gnsssdr is upstream's own standalone SIMD kernel library, shipped inside the
gnss-sdr tarball. It is unrelated to Factory's volk/libvolk3_3 and shares no file
or package name with it. The default flavour BuildRequires gnss-sdr-volk-devel
from the volk flavour of this same source package; OBS schedules the flavours as
separate jobs, which is how it already builds in hardware:sdr.

Cleaned up before submitting:
- the VOLK library subpackage was still named libvolk_gnsssdr0_0_17 while the
  SONAME is libvolk_gnsssdr.so.0.0.21. That failed the build on rpmlint
  shlib-policy-name-error (badness 10000), so the volk flavour had been red since
  the 0.0.21 update and Factory would have hit the same. Renamed to
  libvolk_gnsssdr0_0_21.
- License re-derived per flavour from what each flavour actually compiles and
  installs: upstream is GPL-3.0-or-later, not GPL-3.0-only, and the binaries
  additionally carry LGPL-3.0-only, BSD-1-Clause, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause and
  MIT (default flavour) resp. BSD-3-Clause and Zlib (volk). A Legal-Review-Notice
  above the tag records which tarball components are never built.
- abseil is now build required. It is the logging and flags backend 0.0.21 links,
  while the previously required glog and gflags were unused; abseil is only
  optional to upstream cmake, so losing it from the buildroot would have switched
  the backend silently rather than failing.
- gnuradio dropped from the volk flavour; volk_gnsssdr does not reference it, and
  the dependency made that flavour unresolvable wherever gnuradio is unavailable.
- the default flavour no longer builds the unit tests it then discarded.
- %check runs the VOLK QA suite (47 of 48 ctest cases).
  qa_volk_gnsssdr_32fc_convert_8ic is deselected: it compares the NEON kernel
  against generic at tolerance 0 and trips on a 1 LSB rounding difference on
  some aarch64 workers. A spec comment records why.
- version floors declared for gnuradio (fatal when older) and for armadillo,
  matio and protobuf (older versions make upstream cmake download sources, which
  cannot work in OBS).
- Group tags dropped, %autosetup, %ldconfig_scriptlets, pkgconfig() build deps,
  COPYING shipped in every subpackage, shebangs and stale sidecar bytecode
  removed from the imported volk_gnsssdr_modtool modules.

Both flavours build green in hardware:sdr on x86_64 and aarch64 (revision 6);
rpmlint badness 0 for gnss-sdr and 1 for the volk flavour (invalid-spec-name,
which every multibuild source package emits).</comment>
